  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "The dominant finding is that scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder produces a massive jump (config_011: 0.706 acc) over scgpt (~0.54 acc), making it the critical design choice. Config_011 uses avgpool aggregation, which was also best for scgpt (0.542 vs 0.520 for transformer). However, the interaction between aggregation method and encoder richness is untested: a transformer aggregator may better exploit the richer, learned latent representations from scvi_n200 compared to the simpler scgpt embeddings. Config_013 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal) is a single-parameter exploitation of the best config, testing whether transformer aggregation can push accuracy above 0.706. This is the highest-value next step because it keeps all proven winning components while probing the one dimension where encoder-dependent interaction is uncertain, and with only 3 experiments remaining, a focused exploitation around the current best is the best use of budget."
}

